BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (Linton tells his appointment setters, "I cannot stress to you guys how important it is to be setting follow-ups," and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (names high call volume plus follow-up management as the most important thing in the job [B415KkGunUw @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (00:05:39]. The operator takeaway is consistent: the money sits in the second through sixth touch, so the system has to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (remember the prospect even when the rep does not, and the cadence has to stay polite enough that the buyer keeps) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (picking up.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (The second agreed rule: the ask on the phone or at the door is a walkthrough or a meeting, never a price. Anton Pantio) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (names asking for quotes instead of walk-throughs as the second big mistake owners make, and says his live booking) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (landed because the setter offered a free walkthrough in a relaxed tone at mid-morning, where a 4:30pm dial would have) Tj ET
