BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 429.77 Tm (Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 407.55 Tm (Underbidding is the first wound most operators report. Carolyn Arellano states flatly that newcomers will underbid,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 392.32 Tm (that it happened to them too, and that the fix is timing every task from the first account onward [IJlyq2UAXqU @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 377.10 Tm (00:03:18]. Clean Ops Guide walks the economics: a $2,000 monthly contract looks like a win until wages, supplies,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 361.87 Tm (operating expense and the extra hours spent managing the account leave almost nothing, and shaving a five-hour) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 346.65 Tm (estimate to three hours to look competitive only moves the shortfall into rushed cleaning, employee frustration,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 331.42 Tm (declining quality or the owner working extra hours [9ojOIxznBUc @ 00:01:04]. A $20 hourly wage is not a $20 labor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 316.20 Tm (cost either, once payroll taxes, workers compensation, insurance and training land on top. Karen Denton names the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 300.97 Tm (copy-paste trap, recalling copying franchise bids and watching every client tear those proposals apart [h7lD-HNIQ_o) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 285.75 Tm (@ 00:00:43]. Matt Stowe adds the anchoring error seen across consulting clients: asking a prospect what they pay now) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 270.52 Tm (and setting the price there, or blurting a number off a price list before any due diligence, when the correct answer is that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 255.30 Tm (a lot of questions come first [nBB03PNbUHI @ 00:04:50].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 240.07 Tm (The second cluster is scope blindness on the walkthrough. An OctoClean coach says density is what beginners miss) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 224.85 Tm (most: bidding an open car dealership showroom, where the crew mostly dust mops and mops, the same as a cube farm) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 209.62 Tm (loaded with trash cans and desks ends with an operator asking why they are not making money [45JohGIULbI @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 194.40 Tm (00:00:54]. On the ISSA Media panel, Matt describes the distribution-facility version, bidding cleanable square footage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 179.17 Tm (while ignoring the hour of walking to reach a single restroom on the far side of the building; customers understand) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 163.95 Tm (non-productive time but will not raise it, so the contractor must [nBB03PNbUHI @ 00:05:47]. Bad inputs compound it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 148.72 Tm (A prospect claiming 655,000 square feet turned out to have an 823 square foot office with the rest warehouse, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 133.50 Tm (salespeople incentivized on commission have handed operations accounts with four restrooms nobody counted, which) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 118.27 Tm (is why OctoClean makes reps measure every square inch themselves [zAGjNnpTUcY @ 00:21:16]. Rudy Perez flags) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 103.05 Tm (the gut-versus-formula gap as its own trap: walking a site and sensing five hours a night while the bid math says three) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 87.82 Tm (leaves the number badly off, which is why that operator averages the hourly and square foot results [1_z-Kgj0GYM @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 72.60 Tm (00:03:38].) Tj ET
