BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 509.77 Tm (The most expensive firsthand loss on record comes from OctoClean Media: the hosts did not read the fine print, a job) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 494.55 Tm (carried two or three cleans buried in the scope of work, and the re-cleans cost over $100,000 in labor [9TymiXPWhyY) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 479.32 Tm (@ 00:10:36]. Their rule is to read whether the spec says final cleaning only or final, punch and trade clean before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 464.10 Tm (pricing. The companion trap is the free re-clean. After the architect and construction manager walk the punch list,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 448.87 Tm (trades make a fresh mess, and cleaners who just go back and clean again give away the time-and-materials money that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 433.65 Tm (makes the job lucrative; the fix is a logo sheet marked room completed on each finished door and a daily supervisor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 418.42 Tm (sign-off [YE3spKAx9HI @ 00:03:02]. Mark Etherton owns the same rookie list: underpricing, not walking the first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 403.20 Tm (site, not clarifying scope, not invoicing the same day, and trying to be cheap instead of professional, every one made) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 387.97 Tm (before fixing them paid off in the thousands [PG-8SEuPFQk @ 00:01:36]. Darian Jarrett flipped punch-list churn into) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 372.75 Tm (revenue, billing every in-between touch-up at an average $75 an hour, adding fuel when crews commuted far, and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 357.52 Tm (contractor was totally fine paying that premium [c9LRSgPQlvE @ 00:08:09].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 342.30 Tm (Cash flow is the second killer. The OctoClean hosts warn that many contractors hiring cleaners are third- or fourth-tier) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 327.07 Tm (subs, so payment arrives when theirs does, which can stretch six months or longer, and the contracts need watching) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 311.85 Tm ([9TymiXPWhyY @ 00:02:02]. Darian Jarrett saw a milder version on a first job: terms were net 30 but the check) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 296.62 Tm (landed closer to net 45 or 50, so barrels, mop buckets, mops, brooms, gloves and rags came out of cash reserves while) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 281.40 Tm (the 1st-and-15th payroll still had to clear [c9LRSgPQlvE @ 00:02:49]. Labor whiplash compounds it: OctoClean) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 266.17 Tm (describes supers penalized for running over who demand 25 units today and none tomorrow, forcing crews home,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 250.95 Tm (which is why the hosts keep staff at four to six hours a night plus a bench of short-term workers. OctoClean adds that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 235.72 Tm (ladder work above a certain height or any boom lift pushes workers comp costs higher. Insurance is the next wall.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 220.50 Tm (Construction Clean Partners says 99 percent of its contractors refuse cleaners without workers compensation, though) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 205.27 Tm (jobs worth $10,000 to $30,000 can justify buying it [vx1fwmFh0zM @ 00:02:16]. Jarrett confirms builders) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 190.05 Tm (automatically request a W9, general liability and workers comp before the vendor portal clears [_hqGinSApYg @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 174.82 Tm (00:08:14].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 159.60 Tm (Floor care carries its own failure modes. OctoClean Media warns that a bad strip leaves finish that will not adhere or,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 144.37 Tm (worse, shiny dirt, a bad finish means stripping the floor again, bye-bye profit, and high-alkaline strippers can ruin) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 129.15 Tm (Marmoleum and stick the cleaner with replacing a very expensive surface [X3MX2xOshA4 @ 00:01:56]. The same) Tj ET
